<title>UK: Portugal prices 3.0 bln French franc 10-year bond.</title>
<headline>Portugal prices 3.0 bln French franc 10-year bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond, announced earlier by joint lead managers BNP, CDC Marche and Lehman Brothers, has been priced.</p>
<p> BORROWER   PORTUGAL</p>
<p> AMT    3.0 BLN FFR   COUPON     5.625     MATURITY    03.APR.07</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  100.567   PAY DATE    03.APR.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  2.00	REOFFER    98.892    SPREAD	+17 BP</p>
<p> MOODY	AA3	 LISTING    PARIS     PAY FREQ    =</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  AA-	 DENOMS (K) 10-100-1M SALE LIMITS US/UK/FR</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    FRENCH    HOME CTRY  PORTUGAL  TAX PROVS   STANDARD</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.325     SELL CONC  1.675     PRAECIPUUM  =</p>
<p> UNDERLYING GOVT BOND INTERPOLATED 2006 AND 2007 OATS</p>
<p> NOTES     THE BOND WILL BE REDENOMINATED INTO EUROS AFTER</p>
<p>	     STAGE 3 OF EUROPEAN ECONOMIC AND MONETARY UNION (EMU)</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
